      "writtenOn": "2022-11-17T20:17:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doc comments render differently in many editors versus `//` comments (including in Xcode!), and IDEs can extract them for things like hover tips. \n\nAnyway, we should be consistent--if we want to change these, we should be intentional about it, get a team consensus, and change them all for a class at once instead of changing one at a time when you edit something nearby. Having a mix of styles in one class is ugly.\n\nPlease change back for this CL and take a poll in chat/send an email to the team.",
